{"step_index":111,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:58:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T01:58:41Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T01:58:41Z\nShowing lines 71-140 of 281\n71:     (\"agents\", \"software\"),\n72: ];\n73: \n74: /// Resolve a possibly-aliased category to the OSCAL category it means.\n75: ///\n76: /// Non-aliased values pass through untouched, so this is safe to call on any\n77: /// category — including internal ones, which have no OSCAL equivalent and are\n78: /// deliberately returned as-is rather than forced into the standard vocabulary.\n79: pub fn canonical_category(category: &str) -> &str {\n80:     CATEGORY_ALIASES\n81:         .iter()\n82:         .find(|(alias, _)| *alias == category)\n83:         .map(|(_, oscal)| *oscal)\n84:         .unwrap_or(category)\n85: }\n86: \n87: /// Every accepted value for a subid's second segment: OSCAL, internal, and\n88: /// aliases. Presented to consumers as simply the `category`.\n89: pub fn component_types() -> impl Iterator<Item = &'static str> {\n90:     OSCAL_COMPONENT_TYPES\n91:         .iter()\n92:         .chain(INTERNAL_CATEGORIES.iter())\n93:         .copied()\n94:         .chain(CATEGORY_ALIASES.iter().map(|(alias, _)| *alias))\n95: }\n96: \n97: /// Whether `candidate` is an accepted category from either vocabulary.\n98: pub fn is_component_type(candidate: &str) -> bool {\n99:     component_types().any(|t| t == candidate)\n100: }\n101: \n102: /// Regex validating an OSCAL subid.\n103: ///\n104: /// Shared between the schemars adapter, the canonical subid registry schema,\n105: /// and any runtime validation that wants a single source of truth for the\n106: /// taxonomy format. Built from [`SUBID_CATEGORIES`], [`OSCAL_COMPONENT_TYPES`]\n107: /// and [`INTERNAL_CATEGORIES`] so a vocabulary change cannot leave the regex\n108: /// behind — adding a category is a one-line edit to one list.\n109: pub fn subid_regex() -> &'static str {\n110:     static PATTERN: std::sync::OnceLock<String> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();\n111:     PATTERN.get_or_init(|| {\n112:         let segment = r\"[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*\";\n113:         let types: Vec<&str> = component_types().collect();\n114:         format!(\n115:             r\"^({})\\.({})\\.{segment}\\.{segment}(?:\\.{segment}){{0,2}}(?:@v[1-9][0-9]*)?$\",\n116:             SUBID_CATEGORIES.join(\"|\"),\n117:             types.join(\"|\"),\n118:         )\n119:     })\n120: }\n121: \n122: /// Validate a subid string against the canonical regex.\n123: pub fn validate_subid(subid: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n124:     static RE: std::sync::OnceLock<Regex> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();\n125:     let re = RE.get_or_init(|| Regex::new(subid_regex()).expect(\"subid_regex is valid\"));\n126:     if re.is_match(subid) {\n127:         Ok(())\n128:     } else {\n129:         Err(format!(\"subid does not match required pattern: {subid}\"))\n130:     }\n131: }\n132: \n133: /// Return the metadata fields that are required for a given subid category.\n134: ///\n135: /// Per AGENTS.md §4a:\n136: /// - `mut` requires `actor_id` and `capability_id`\n137: /// - `evt` requires `event_id` or `event_hash`\n138: /// - `src` requires `source_system` and `source_locator`\n139: /// - all other categories have no additional required metadata fields\n140: pub fn category_required_fields(category: &str) -> &'static [&'static str] {"}
{"step_index":112,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:58:42Z","input_tokens":2309,"cache_read_tokens":95968,"output_tokens":848,"thinking":"Examining the provided code reveals three distinct category definitions. These categories likely represent classifications within a system, potentially for identifying and organizing different elements. Specific aliases map certain terms to more general categories, indicating possible data normalization or a need for simplified categorization.\n\n\n\"Subsidiary\" can be a component type within the taxonomy, potentially categorized under internal components or aliased to existing OSCAL component types such as \"system\" or \"interconnection\". Alternatively, it could denote an organizational hierarchy tag, reflecting the conglomerate structure. It also needs consideration within the SUBID categories.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":60,"Path":"/srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/oscal_subid_registry.rs","StartLine":1}}]}
{"step_index":113,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:58:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T01:58:50Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T01:58:50Z\nShowing lines 1-60 of 605\n1: //! OSCAL Subid Registry plugin — sealed subid discovery and review metadata.\n2: //!\n3: //! Every D-Bus object, plugin, schema, mutation, event, and tool carries two\n4: //! identifiers: a `uuid` (machine identity) and a `subid` (human-readable\n5: //! operational taxonomy key). Runtime membership comes only from the sealed\n6: //! plugin catalog; this plugin can annotate an existing subid but cannot mint\n7: //! one.\n8: //!\n9: //! Compliance refs live in metadata arrays — never inside the subid string itself.\n10: \n11: use anyhow::{Result, bail};\n12: use op_state::{ApplyResult, Checkpoint, PluginCapabilities, StateDiff, StatePlugin};\n13: use op_state_store::PluginSchema;\n14: use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n15: use simd_json::OwnedValue as Value;\n16: \n17: use super::oscal_field_classification::{ASSESS_CAPABILITY, AssessFieldsInput, FieldAssessment};\n18: use super::oscal_subid_registry_methods::{\n19:     ExportInput, ExportOutput, ListByCategoryInput, ListByCategoryOutput, LookupInput,\n20:     LookupOutput, RegisterInput, RegisterOutput, ResolveInput, ResolveOutput,\n21: };\n22: \n23: // ── Defaults for serde ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: \n25: fn default_version() -> u32 {\n26:     1\n27: }\n28: \n29: fn default_authority_rank() -> i64 {\n30:     100\n31: }\n32: \n33: // ── Examples for schemars ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n34: \n35: fn example_uuid() -> String {\n36:     \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef0123456789\".to_string()\n37: }\n38: \n39: fn example_subid() -> String {\n40:     \"mut.service.state-sync.apply-patch@v1\".to_string()\n41: }\n42: \n43: fn example_category() -> OscalSubidCategory {\n44:     OscalSubidCategory::Mut\n45: }\n46: \n47: fn example_component_type() -> OscalComponentType {\n48:     OscalComponentType::Service\n49: }\n50: \n51: fn example_subject() -> String {\n52:     \"state-sync\".to_string()\n53: }\n54: \n55: fn example_verb() -> String {\n56:     \"apply-patch\".to_string()\n57: }\n58: \n59: fn example_facet() -> Option<String> {\n60:     Some(\"rollback\".to_string())"}
