{"step_index":127,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:01:52Z","input_tokens":2825,"cache_read_tokens":104956,"output_tokens":1010,"content":"**Yes, absolutely.** Axum is designed so you can host completely isolated sites within the same application.\n\nHere are the three primary ways Axum handles isolated sites:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Isolated Subdomains / Virtual Hosts (`Host` Matching)\nAxum can inspect the HTTP `Host` header to serve completely different router trees for different domains (e.g., `3tched.com` vs `hack.3tched.com`):\n\n```rust\nuse axum::{Router, extract::Host, response::Response, routing::get};\n\n// Router for the main parent site\nfn root_site() -> Router { ... }\n\n// Completely isolated router for the subsidiary\nfn hackathon_site() -> Router { ... }\n\nlet app = Router::new().fallback(|host: Host, req| async move {\n    if host.0.starts_with(\"hack.\") {\n        hackathon_site().oneshot(req).await\n    } else {\n        root_site().oneshot(req).await\n    }\n});\n```\n* **Paired with Xray:** Xray terminates TLS and demuxes via SNI/Host, forwarding the request to Axum, which dispatches it to the subsidiary's private site handler.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Path-Prefixed Site Nesting (`Router::nest`)\nIf both sites live under the same domain, Axum can isolate them by path prefix:\n\n```rust\nlet app = Router::new()\n    .nest_service(\"/\", ServeDir::new(\"/usr/local/share/op-dbus/dashboard/prod\"))\n    .nest_service(\"/hack\", ServeDir::new(\"/home/jeremy/projects/hack-3tched/dist\"));\n```\n* Each `.nest()` can carry its **own independent state (`State`)**, its own middleware, authentication gates, and asset directories. State from the parent does not bleed into the nested site unless explicitly shared.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Multiple Listeners / Ports\nA single Axum binary can bind to multiple ports or sockets simultaneously:\n* **Port 8080:** System / Public dashboard\n* **Port 8086:** Subsidiary hackathon dashboard\n\nEach port runs its own `axum::serve` loop with a completely separate `Router` instance and zero shared memory.","thinking":"Axum itself does not inherently provide site isolation. Domain awareness, essential for isolating sites, is handled by the Xray gateway. Therefore, Axum relies on Xray's domain demultiplexing to route requests to the appropriate isolated site based on the incoming domain. This architecture enables site isolation within the system.\n\n\n"}
