{"step_index":133,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:04:30Z","input_tokens":3238,"cache_read_tokens":108053,"output_tokens":991,"content":"**That is the cleanest possible security boundary.**\n\nBecause **3tchedFS acts as the lungs** for the instance, all communication with backend services, memory, plugins, and state happens locally through the kernel VFS layer via file I/O—not over TCP sockets.\n\nThis completely simplifies the networking model:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Zero-Internal-Network Model\n\n```\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │               SUBSIDIARY (hack:3tched)                  │\n   └────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬────────────┘\n                │                               │\n        [ FUSE Filesystem ]             [ Outbound WAN Only ]\n                │                               │\n                ▼                               ▼\n    /run/mounts/3tchedFS/             Public Internet\n    • Operations & tool calls         • External API queries\n    • Memory queries / storage        • Web scraping / research\n    • State inspection                • Package downloads\n                │\n                ▼\n      [ Internal Host Services ]\n      (Zero TCP ports exposed)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is Architecturally Superior\n\n1. **Zero Host Attack Surface:**\n   * The instance does not need access to `10.0.0.2:8090`, `:8080`, `:6333` (Qdrant), or `:1883` (EMQX) over the network.\n   * Internal host loopback and LAN can be **100% blocked**. Port-scanning from inside the instance yields nothing.\n\n2. **No Network Credential Leaks:**\n   * No API tokens, bearer tokens, or database passwords ever transit over a local network socket.\n   * Identity is verified at the filesystem boundary by kernel file ownership and the mounted FUSE session.\n\n3. **Trivial Firewalling:**\n   The network policy for the user/container becomes a simple one-liner:\n   * **Drop** all packets destined for private/local IP ranges (`127.0.0.0/8`, `10.0.0.0/8`, `192.168.0.0/16`, `172.16.0.0/12`).\n   * **Allow** standard public Internet egress (HTTP/HTTPS/DNS).\n\nAll operational power flows through file operations in the mounted 3tchedFS, while the network provides only external internet access for the hackathon tasks.","thinking":"The user's statement suggests a significant architectural shift. The system no longer requires internal network connectivity for services exposed on specific ports; all internal communication now occurs via the FUSE filesystem. Consequently, the only required network connection is for internet access.\n\n\n"}
